-- title:
--   Lifting integral mod-q modular functions to characteristic zero
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (realised as `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`), $N$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid N$, and $k$ a field of characteristic $q$ equipped with a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$. Write $F_M(C)$ for the intermediate field `modularFunctionFieldC C N` of $C$-Laurent series generated over a field $C$ by `jqModC C` (the series $q^{-1}\cdot(\text{the integral } j\text{-numerator reduced to } C)$) and by its $N$-fold substitution `jqNModC C N = qExpand C N (jqModC C)`. Given $h_0 \in F_M(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ and $\bar g \in F_M(k)$ such that the coefficientwise image of $h_0$ under $\mathbb{Z}/q \to k$ equals $\bar g$, and such that $\bar g$ is integral over the $k$-subalgebra of $F_M(k)$ generated by `jGeomGen k N` $=$ `jqModC k` and `jNGeomGen k N` $=$ `jqNModC k N`, the conclusion produces a Laurent series $g_0$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, a Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$, and an element $g$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar N`, the field generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series by the coefficientwise images of `modularFunctionFieldFull N` $= \mathbb{Q}(\,\mathrm{qExpand}_{\mathbb{Q},d}\,j_q : d \mid N,\ d \neq 0)$, such that: $g_0$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldFull N`; $g$, viewed as a Laurent series, is the coefficientwise image `coeffEmb` of $g_0$; the coefficientwise image of $y$ under $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is likewise `coeffEmb` of $g_0$ (so $g_0$ has all coefficients in $A$); the coefficientwise image of $h_0$ in $k$ coincides with the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ along $\mathrm{red}$; and $g$ is integral over the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subalgebra of `modularFunctionFieldBar N` generated by the images of $j_q$ and of $\mathrm{qExpand}_{\mathbb{Q},N}\, j_q$.
--
--   This is the lifting step expressing good reduction of the modular curve of level $N$ at a prime $q \nmid N$ in the language of $q$-expansions: a function in the characteristic-$q$ modular function field that is integral over the affine coordinate ring $k[\tilde j, \tilde j_N]$ is the reduction of a characteristic-zero modular function with coefficients in the valuation ring $A$ and integral over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}[j, j_N]$. It feeds the construction of specialisations of places of the modular function field used later in the argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_full_lift_isIntegral_of_isIntegral.lean

